# Wrangler loads .dev.vars for local-only values. Phase 2's local loopback
# identity does not require credentials, so this file is intentionally empty.
# Never place Google OAuth or future Facebook/Discord secrets in a VITE_* value.

# Local development does not need an allowlist: `npm run dev:full` runs with
# APP_ENV=local on a loopback host and never verifies a Firebase token. The real
# value belongs in `wrangler secret put APPROVED_EMAILS`, never in a committed
# file. The line below is commented out on purpose, so copying this file to
# .dev.vars changes no behaviour. The addresses are dummies.
#
# APPROVED_EMAILS=["owner@example.com","tester@example.com"]
